From a4a599724e15ed4730ded8b14be8e107f5f0d8b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:50:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] inrun (scratch): body=LIST -- bed births inherit and
 mutate the body genes

Off by default (byte-identical). With body=, a child takes its parent's open
genes and mutates them by creature::inherit_body (the game's birth rule);
closed genes stay the founding body's and take no draw. body=default opens
appetite, digest_rate, crop_capacity, gut_bias, pace. Bodies carry between
rounds as final/ID.body.txt beside ID.raw.txt; body.csv logs every ant's
open genes at founding and birth.

Checks (hA1, sel=score, ha1next args):
- 17 genes opened at width 0.5 (birth_grant, reproduce_at, sight_range,
  curvature_radius, the 11 walk/trail genes, the 2 door genes) moved by up
  to 0.58 and changed nothing: events/births/sel byte-identical to body off
  at 200k frames on seeds 1 and 2 (229 and 308 births). A mind ant never
  reads them.
- Each of appetite (with digest_bar=3), digest_rate, crop_capacity,
  gut_bias, pace, armour, dig_force opened alone changes events.csv within
  40k frames (positive control).
- rounds.sh carries bodies: all 24 round-1 founders match a round-0 final
  body.

Jobs body1022: hA1 64 seeds x 6 rounds, five arms (control, body=default,
body=appetite, hungergate=1, hungergate=1 + body=default).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
